 34AL    PB(35AL,34ALNG)               2017CH36                  ENSDF    202609
 34AL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34AL c  Coulomb dissociation of {+35}Al on Pb target                           
 34AL c  2017Ch36,2014ChZZ: {+35}Al was produced via the projectile             
 34AL2c  fragmentation of a 531-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar primary beam from the Heavy 
 34AL3c  Ion Synchrotron (SIS18) at GSI. The secondary cocktail beam was        
 34AL4c  separated by the FRS separator and impinged on a 2 g/cm{+2} Pb target  
 34AL5c  and a 0.93 g/cm{+2} C target. Projectiles and reaction fragments were  
 34AL6c  detected using 8 DSSDs, separated by a large-area dipole magnet        
 34AL7c  (ALADIN) and tracked using two large scintillator fiber detectors      
 34AL8c  (GFIs). Neutrons from the excited projectiles were detected using the  
 34AL9c  high-efficiency Large Area Neutron Detector (LAND). |g rays from the   
 34ALAc  deexcited projectile and projectile-like fragments were detected using 
 34ALBc  a spherical 4|p Crystal Ball detector array of 162 NaI(Tl) crystals.   
 34ALCc  Measured E(fragment), E{-n}, E|g, Coulomb dissociation cross sections. 
 34ALDc  Deduced relative populations of {+34}Al, {+35}Al g.s. configuration.   
 34ALEc  Comparisons with shell-model calculations with the SDPF-M interaction. 
 34ALFc  The measured inclusive differential CD cross section (integrated up to 
 34ALGc  5.0 MeV relative energy) for {+35}Al|){+34}Al+n using a Pb target is 78
 34ALHc  mb {I13}.                                                              
 34AL c  2021Bh12: A further analysis of the data from 2017Ch36. The            
 34AL2c  {+35}Al(|g,n){+34}Al photoabsorption cross section was obtained from   
 34AL3c  fitting the direct breakup model to the measured differential Coulomb  
 34AL4c  dissociation cross section of {+35}Al breaking up into {+34}Al core    
 34AL5c  excited states. The {+34}Al(n,|g){+35}Al neutron capture cross sections
 34AL6c  were obtained from the photoabsorption cross sections using the        
 34AL7c  detailed balance theorem.                                              
 34AL cG E$From level-energy difference, as indicated in Fig. 2(c) of 2017Ch36  
 34AL cL $Partial level scheme and half-lives are as given in 2017Ch36, taken   
 34AL2cL from 2017Li03: Phys Rev C 95, 021301(R) (2017), unless otherwise noted.
 34AL3cL Energy values are rounded-off values.                                  
 34AL cL $The total measured inclusive differential Coulomb dissociation cross  
 34AL2cL section is 78 mb {I13}, integrated up to 5.0 MeV relative energy       
 34AL3cL between the {+34}Al core and the neutron using a Pb target.            
